  "text": "Branded-residence development in the **Caribbean and Latin America (CALA)** is concentrated among luxury and upper-upscale hospitality brands. The names most commonly encountered—across completed projects and the development pipeline—include:\n\n### Leading brands\n\n- **The Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve** — Marriott  \n- **Four Seasons**\n- **St. Regis** — Marriott  \n- **Rosewood**\n- **Autograph Collection** — Marriott  \n- **W Hotels** — Marriott  \n- **Waldorf Astoria** — Hilton  \n\nRecent industry reporting identifies Ritz-Carlton as the regional leader, with Four Seasons, St. Regis, Rosewood, Autograph Collection, W and Waldorf Astoria also among the most active brands. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Branded-Residences-Americas-report.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Other established luxury operators\n\n- **Aman**\n- **Mandarin Oriental**\n- **Fairmont** — Accor  \n- **One&Only**\n- **Six Senses** — IHG  \n- **Auberge Resorts Collection**\n- **Montage / Pendry**\n- **Park Hyatt and Andaz** — Hyatt  \n- **Conrad** — Hilton  \n- **EDITION, JW Marriott, The Luxury Collection and Westin** — Marriott  \n- **Belmond**\n- **Banyan Tree**\n- **Nobu Hotels**\n\nThese brands appear less uniformly across the region but are particularly visible in Mexico, Costa Rica, the Dominican Republic, Puerto Rico, the Bahamas and selected South American gateway and resort markets. ([guide.lprluxury.com](https://guide.lprluxury.com/guide?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Regionally important names\n\n- **Fasano** — especially in Brazil and Uruguay  \n- **Chablé** — Mexico  \n- Various independent luxury-resort brands that use a hotel-management or rental-program model  \n\nHistorically, **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, Rosewood and Aman** have been especially associated with Caribbean resort residences, while Latin America has a broader mix of global hotel brands, regional hospitality operators and lifestyle/design brands. ([readkong.com](https://www.readkong.com/page/branded-residences-savills-8636984?utm_source=openai))\n\nIn practical terms, the five names most likely to appear in a CALA branded-residence competitive set are **Ritz-Carlton, Four Seasons, St. Regis, Rosewood and Autograph Collection**. Marriott has the broadest multi-brand presence in the sector.",
